# UI Polish Always

Apply this standard to every UI change in this repo (standard, minimal, log-first, HUD).

- Keep launch usable without fullscreen; primary actions must be visible.
- Favor compact, scannable layouts: reduce dead space and preserve hierarchy.
- Maintain strong contrast for helper/status text in all themes.
- Keep spacing and control sizes consistent across modes.
- Add hover/focus/pressed states for interactive controls.
- Preserve responsiveness during resize; avoid expensive reflow loops.
- When adding controls, persist user-facing preferences where reasonable.
- Prefer deterministic layout behavior over auto-magic that jumps unexpectedly.
- Validate by compile + lints after UI edits.

Quick checklist before finishing:
- Primary workflow visible at launch
- No clipping/overlap at common sizes
- No stuck cursor or resize lockups
- Theme parity (standard/minimal/log-first/HUD)
